    "notes": "- feat(cs): outbound reply filter in shadow mode — flags openclaw noise (model-fallback banners, reasoning residue, tool/provider errors, internal paths) in AI replies to customers\n- Shadow mode only records; replies are never altered or blocked. It hangs off the existing cs-event mirror, so it adds no latency to the send path and needs no plugin change or gateway restart\n- New Customer Service → Settings card: shadow toggle, hit counts, per-rule tallies, and a per-hit diff of what the customer received vs what an enforcing filter would have sent\n- 'enforce' mode is stored but not yet settable — enforcing requires the plugin's message_sending hook to await a verdict",
